{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"laravel-migrations","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Laravel Migrations","description":"Build migration column lines with modifiers, foreign keys and indexes from pickers, and start a migration from a plain sentence like \"add status to orders\".","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:laravelMigrations.column","onCommand:laravelMigrations.foreignKey","onCommand:laravelMigrations.indexLine","onCommand:laravelMigrations.dropColumnLine","onCommand:laravelMigrations.newFromSentence"],"permissions":["terminal"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"laravelMigrations.column","title":"Insert Column...","category":"Laravel Migrations"},{"command":"laravelMigrations.foreignKey","title":"Insert Foreign Key...","category":"Laravel Migrations"},{"command":"laravelMigrations.indexLine","title":"Insert Index...","category":"Laravel Migrations"},{"command":"laravelMigrations.dropColumnLine","title":"Insert Drop Column...","category":"Laravel Migrations"},{"command":"laravelMigrations.newFromSentence","title":"New Migration from a Sentence...","category":"Laravel Migrations"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"laravelMigrations.column","key":"Ctrl+Alt+C"}],"configuration":{"title":"Laravel Migrations","properties":{"laravelMigrations.runner":{"type":"string","default":"php artisan","description":"What starts artisan: \"php artisan\", \"./vendor/bin/sail artisan\" or \"docker compose exec app php artisan\"."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Laravel Migrations: build column lines for a migration, add foreign keys and indexes, and start a new migration from a plain sentence.\n\nconst COLUMN_TYPES = [\n  ['string', 'VARCHAR (default 255)', 'length'], ['text', 'TEXT'], ['longText', 'LONGTEXT'], ['integer', 'INT'], ['bigInteger', 'BIGINT'], ['unsignedBigInteger', 'unsigned BIGINT'], ['boolean', 'true or false'],\n  ['decimal', 'exact number, asks for digits', 'decimal'], ['float', 'floating point'], ['date', 'a date'], ['dateTime', 'date and time'], ['timestamp', 'a timestamp'], ['json', 'JSON data'], ['uuid', 'UUID'], ['ulid', 'ULID'],\n  ['enum', 'one of a list', 'enum'], ['foreignId', 'a foreign key id'], ['id', 'auto increment primary key'], ['timestamps', 'created_at and updated_at'], ['softDeletes', 'deleted_at for soft deletes'], ['rememberToken', 'remember_token'], ['morphs', 'type and id for a polymorphic relation'], ['binary', 'binary data'], ['ipAddress', 'an IP address'],\n];\nconst NO_NAME = new Set(['id', 'timestamps', 'softDeletes', 'rememberToken']);\nconst MODIFIERS = [['nullable', 'allow NULL'], ['unique', 'unique index'], ['index', 'plain index'], ['default', 'a default value', 'value'], ['unsigned', 'unsigned number'], ['after', 'place after a column', 'column'], ['comment', 'a comment', 'text'], ['useCurrent', 'default to now']];\n\nconst IDENT = /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$/;\nconst q = (s) => \"'\" + String(s).replace(/\\\\/g, '\\\\\\\\').replace(/'/g, \"\\\\'\") + \"'\";\nconst literal = (v) => (/^(true|false|null|-?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?)$/i.test(v) ? v.toLowerCase() : q(v));\n\n/** One column line, for example $table->string('name', 100)->nullable()->unique(); */\nfunction columnLine(o) {\n  const type = o.type;\n  if (!COLUMN_TYPES.some((t) => t[0] === type)) throw new Error('Unknown column type ' + type);\n  let args = '';\n  if (!NO_NAME.has(type)) {\n    if (!IDENT.test(o.name || '')) throw new Error('A column name uses letters, digits and underscores, and does not start with a digit.');\n    args = q(o.name);\n    if (type === 'string' && o.length) args += ', ' + Number(o.length);\n    if (type === 'decimal' && o.precision) args += ', ' + Number(o.precision) + ', ' + Number(o.scale ?? 2);\n    if (type === 'enum') args += ', [' + (o.values || []).map(q).join(', ') + ']';\n  } else if (type === 'softDeletes' && o.name) args = q(o.name);\n  let line = '$table->' + type + '(' + args + ')';\n  for (const m of o.modifiers || []) {\n    if (!MODIFIERS.some((x) => x[0] === m.name)) throw new Error('Unknown modifier ' + m.name);\n    line += '->' + m.name + '(' + (m.value !== undefined && m.value !== '' ? (m.name === 'after' || m.name === 'comment' ? q(m.value) : literal(m.value)) : '') + ')';\n  }\n  return line + ';';\n}\n\n/** A foreign key: foreignId('user_id')->constrained()->cascadeOnDelete(); */\nfunction foreignLine(o) {\n  if (!IDENT.test(o.column || '')) throw new Error('The column name is not valid.');\n  let line = \"$table->foreignId('\" + o.column + \"')\";\n  if (o.nullable) line += '->nullable()';\n  line += o.table ? '->constrained(' + q(o.table) + ')' : '->constrained()';\n  if (o.onDelete === 'cascade') line += '->cascadeOnDelete()';\n  else if (o.onDelete === 'null') line += '->nullOnDelete()';\n  else if (o.onDelete === 'restrict') line += '->restrictOnDelete()';\n  return line + ';';\n}\n\nconst words = (s) => s.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9 _,]+/g, ' ').replace(/_/g, ' ').trim();\nconst snakeWords = (s) => s.trim().split(/\\s+/).join('_');\n\n/**\n * \"create orders table\", \"add status and total to orders\", \"remove notes from orders\", \"rename users to members\", \"drop logs\"\n * become a migration name and the artisan options Laravel uses to prefill the file.\n */\nfunction migrationFromSentence(sentence) {\n  const s = words(sentence).replace(/\\b(table|column|columns|field|fields)\\b/g, '').replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n  let m = /^(?:create|make|new)\\s+(?:an?\\s+|the\\s+)?(\\w+)$/.exec(s);\n  if (m) return { name: 'create_' + m[1] + '_table', args: ['--create=' + m[1]], summary: 'Create the ' + m[1] + ' table' };\n  m = /^(?:add|adds)\\s+(.+?)\\s+(?:to|on|in)\\s+(?:the\\s+)?(\\w+)$/.exec(s);\n  if (m) {\n    const cols = m[1].split(/\\s*(?:,|\\band\\b)\\s*/).filter(Boolean).map(snakeWords);\n    return { name: 'add_' + cols.join('_and_') + '_to_' + m[2] + '_table', args: ['--table=' + m[2]], summary: 'Add ' + cols.join(', ') + ' to ' + m[2], columns: cols };\n  }\n  m = /^(?:remove|drop|delete)\\s+(.+?)\\s+from\\s+(?:the\\s+)?(\\w+)$/.exec(s);\n  if (m) {\n    const cols = m[1].split(/\\s*(?:,|\\band\\b)\\s*/).filter(Boolean).map(snakeWords);\n    return { name: 'remove_' + cols.join('_and_') + '_from_' + m[2] + '_table', args: ['--table=' + m[2]], summary: 'Remove ' + cols.join(', ') + ' from ' + m[2], columns: cols, drop: true };\n  }\n  m = /^rename\\s+(\\w+)\\s+to\\s+(\\w+)$/.exec(s);\n  if (m) return { name: 'rename_' + m[1] + '_to_' + m[2] + '_table', args: [], summary: 'Rename ' + m[1] + ' to ' + m[2] };\n  m = /^(?:drop|delete)\\s+(\\w+)$/.exec(s);\n  if (m) return { name: 'drop_' + m[1] + '_table', args: ['--table=' + m[1]], summary: 'Drop the ' + m[1] + ' table' };\n  m = /^(?:add\\s+)?(?:an?\\s+)?(?:index|indexes)\\s+(?:on|to)\\s+(\\w+)\\s+(?:on|for)\\s+(\\w+)$/.exec(s);\n  if (m) return { name: 'add_index_to_' + m[2] + '_' + m[1] + '_table', args: ['--table=' + m[2]], summary: 'Index ' + m[1] };\n  return null;\n}\n\n/** The body of up() and down() a sentence suggests, so the file starts useful. */\nfunction suggestedBody(info) {\n  if (!info || !info.columns) return null;\n  const t = info.args[0].split('=')[1];\n  if (info.drop) return { up: info.columns.map((c) => \"$table->dropColumn('\" + c + \"');\"), down: info.columns.map((c) => \"$table->string('\" + c + \"')->nullable();\"), table: t };\n  return { up: info.columns.map((c) => \"$table->string('\" + c + \"')->nullable();\"), down: info.columns.map((c) => \"$table->dropColumn('\" + c + \"');\"), table: t };\n}\n\nexports._test = { columnLine, foreignLine, migrationFromSentence, suggestedBody, COLUMN_TYPES, q };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  const runArtisan = async (cmd, args) => {\n    const prefix = String(ferrum.settings.get('laravelMigrations.runner') || 'php artisan');\n    if (!/^(php artisan|\\.\\/vendor\\/bin\\/sail artisan|docker compose exec app php artisan)$/.test(prefix)) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Unsupported runner setting.', 'error');\n    await ferrum.terminal.run(prefix + ' ' + cmd + ' ' + args.join(' '));\n  };\n\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelMigrations.column', async () => {\n      const t = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(COLUMN_TYPES.map(([label, detail]) => ({ label, detail })), { placeholder: 'Column type' });\n      if (!t) return;\n      const o = { type: t.label, modifiers: [] };\n      if (!NO_NAME.has(t.label)) {\n        const name = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Column name', placeholder: 'title' });\n        if (!name) return;\n        o.name = name.trim();\n        if (t.label === 'string') {\n          const len = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Length (empty for the default 255)', value: '' });\n          if (len === undefined) return;\n          if (/^\\d+$/.test(len)) o.length = len;\n        }\n        if (t.label === 'decimal') {\n          const p = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Precision and scale', value: '8,2' });\n          if (!p) return;\n          const [a, b] = p.split(',').map((x) => x.trim());\n          if (!/^\\d+$/.test(a || '') || (b && !/^\\d+$/.test(b))) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Use two numbers like 8,2.', 'error');\n          o.precision = a;\n          o.scale = b || '2';\n        }\n        if (t.label === 'enum') {\n          const v = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Allowed values, separated by commas', placeholder: 'draft,published,archived' });\n          if (!v) return;\n          o.values = v.split(',').map((x) => x.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n        }\n        const picked = [];\n        while (true) {\n          const remaining = MODIFIERS.filter(([n]) => !picked.includes(n));\n          const items = [{ label: 'Done', detail: picked.length ? '->' + picked.join('()->') + '()' : 'No modifiers' }, ...remaining.map(([n, d]) => ({ label: n, detail: d }))];\n          const c = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(items, { placeholder: 'Add a modifier, or Done' });\n          if (!c) return;\n          if (c.label === 'Done') break;\n          picked.push(c.label);\n          const def = MODIFIERS.find(([n]) => n === c.label);\n          if (def[2]) {\n            const v = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Value for ' + c.label + (def[2] === 'column' ? ' (a column name)' : '') });\n            if (v === undefined) return;\n            o.modifiers.push({ name: c.label, value: v });\n          } else o.modifiers.push({ name: c.label });\n        }\n      }\n      try {\n        await ferrum.editor.insert(columnLine(o));\n      } catch (e) {\n        ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'error');\n      }\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelMigrations.foreignKey', async () => {\n      const column = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Column name', placeholder: 'user_id' });\n      if (!column) return;\n      const guess = column.replace(/_id$/, '');\n      const table = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Table it points to (empty to let Laravel guess from the column)', value: '' });\n      if (table === undefined) return;\n      const onDelete = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick([{ label: 'cascade', detail: 'delete the rows too' }, { label: 'null', detail: 'set the column to NULL (needs nullable)' }, { label: 'restrict', detail: 'block the delete' }, { label: 'none', detail: 'database default' }], { placeholder: 'When the parent is deleted' });\n      if (!onDelete) return;\n      try {\n        await ferrum.editor.insert(foreignLine({ column, table: table || '', nullable: onDelete.label === 'null', onDelete: onDelete.label }));\n        void guess;\n      } catch (e) {\n        ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'error');\n      }\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelMigrations.newFromSentence', async () => {\n      const s = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'What should the migration do?', placeholder: 'add status and total to orders' });\n      if (!s) return;\n      const info = migrationFromSentence(s);\n      if (!info) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Try: \"create orders table\", \"add status and total to orders\", \"remove notes from orders\", \"rename users to members\" or \"drop logs\".', 'warn');\n      if (!(await ferrum.window.confirm('Run: artisan make:migration ' + info.name + ' ' + info.args.join(' ') + '   (' + info.summary + ')', 'Create'))) return;\n      await runArtisan('make:migration', [info.name, ...info.args]);\n      const body = suggestedBody(info);\n      if (body) ferrum.window.showMessage('Created. Suggested lines for up(): ' + body.up.join(' '));\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelMigrations.dropColumnLine', async () => {\n      const name = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Column(s) to drop, comma separated' });\n      if (!name) return;\n      const cols = name.split(',').map((x) => x.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n      if (cols.some((c) => !IDENT.test(c))) return ferrum.window.showMessage('A column name uses letters, digits and underscores.', 'error');\n      await ferrum.editor.insert(cols.length === 1 ? \"$table->dropColumn('\" + cols[0] + \"');\" : '$table->dropColumn([' + cols.map(q).join(', ') + ']);');\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelMigrations.indexLine', async () => {\n      const kind = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick([{ label: 'index' }, { label: 'unique' }, { label: 'fullText' }, { label: 'primary' }], { placeholder: 'Index type' });\n      if (!kind) return;\n      const cols = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Column(s), comma separated', placeholder: 'email' });\n      if (!cols) return;\n      const list = cols.split(',').map((x) => x.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n      if (list.some((c) => !IDENT.test(c))) return ferrum.window.showMessage('A column name uses letters, digits and underscores.', 'error');\n      await ferrum.editor.insert('$table->' + kind.label + '(' + (list.length === 1 ? q(list[0]) : '[' + list.map(q).join(', ') + ']') + ');');\n    }),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Laravel Migrations\n\n- **Insert Column...** (Ctrl+Alt+C) picks the type (string, text, integer, bigInteger, boolean, decimal, date, dateTime, timestamp, json, uuid, ulid, enum, foreignId, id, timestamps, softDeletes, morphs...), asks the name and the extra values (length, decimal precision, enum values), then the modifiers (`nullable`, `unique`, `index`, `default`, `unsigned`, `after`, `comment`, `useCurrent`). Result: `$table->string('title', 100)->nullable()->unique();`\n- **Insert Foreign Key...** writes `$table->foreignId('user_id')->constrained()->cascadeOnDelete();` with the delete behavior you choose.\n- **Insert Index...** and **Insert Drop Column...** for `index`, `unique`, `fullText`, `primary` and `dropColumn`.\n- **New Migration from a Sentence...** understands `create orders table`, `add status and total to orders`, `remove notes from orders`, `rename users to members`, `drop logs`. It shows the artisan command (for example `make:migration add_status_and_total_to_orders_table --table=orders`), asks, runs it in the terminal and suggests the lines for `up()`.\n\nNames are checked (letters, digits and underscores) before they are written or sent to the terminal. Permission: terminal.\n"}}}